FILED s531a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-01) from #1815's probes.  PRE-EXISTING (ade297e7 the same).

REPRO (perl 5.40.3), lib/DiesMod.pm = `package DiesMod; die "dm\n"; 1;`:
  use lib 'lib';
  eval { require DiesMod }; print "err=$@"; print exists $INC{'DiesMod.pm'} ? 1 : 0, defined $INC{'DiesMod.pm'} ? 1 : 0, "\n";
  eval { require DiesMod }; print "again=$@";
perl: err=dm / Compilation failed in require at ...  10  again=Attempt to reload DiesMod.pm aborted. / Compilation failed in require ...
PCL:  err=dm  00  again=dm   -- the module body runs a SECOND time (every side effect twice: a silent wrong for a module that registers, pushes or prints at load).

Two halves: (1) a failed load stores $INC{NAME} = undef (p-use / p-require-file / the hook path; `exists` true, `defined` false); (2) a require that finds an undef entry dies "Attempt to reload NAME aborted.\nCompilation failed in require" (perl's message text is not a goal; the die is).  The "Compilation failed in require" suffix on the FIRST die is text only.  Probe: s531a scratch/s531a/pr/diesmod.pl.  NOTE the #1688 half is separate: a file that returns FALSE leaves %INC ABSENT in perl (probed), which PCL now matches.

=== DONE (s532b) ===
FIXED (cl/pcl-runtime.lisp, commit 'require family'): %p-require-run is the ONE load step p-use and p-require-file share -- %p-require-guard runs the load and, on a perl die escaping it (p-die-error but not p-xs-no-artifact, p-exception), stores $INC{KEY} = undef and re-dies MSG . "Compilation failed in require" at the require's own location (pp_ctl.c S_pop_eval_context_maybe_croak action 2; an object die is stringified as perl's croak does); a non-perl CL error leaves the undef entry and propagates unchanged (its backtrace is the diagnosis).  %p-inc-loaded-p is the 'already loaded?' test of both entries: a defined entry = loaded, an undef one dies "Attempt to reload KEY aborted.\nCompilation failed in require" -- the file never runs twice (probe: runs=1, was 4).  A false file leaves KEY absent; a hook's own entry is deleted then (%p-require-true-or-die).  The hook path and an explicit path go through the same step.  Guard Pl/t/require-value-01.t row 3 (perl oracle; FAILS on 59317afd).  ir-spec 9.0c.  comp/require.t rows: see the session-log section.
